      "message": "This would prevent UAF for `GetInstance` calls following the execution of the exit handler, but it doesn\u0027t protect against `GetInstance` calls that are racing with the handler - e.g. some thread just called `GetInstance` but is not done using the tracer instance.\n\nI\u0027m not sure how to make this thread safe short of ref counting the instance.\n\nIs the `!leakTracer` behavior actually required?  The easy fix for Chromium would be to just leak the tracer.",
